## Constraints & Guidelines

### What NOT to Do
- ❌ **NEVER** hardcode credentials/tokens
- ❌ **NEVER** log sensitive data (passwords, OTP codes, full SSNs by default)
- ❌ **NEVER** use `process.exit()` in application code (handle gracefully)
- ❌ **NEVER** skip `releasePage()` in finally blocks (resource leak)
- ❌ **NEVER** introduce new dependencies without justification
- ❌ **NEVER** use heavy navigation waits (`networkidle`) unless critical
- ❌ **NEVER** bypass the OTP mutex (race conditions)
- ❌ **NEVER** commit `.env`, `tokens.json`, `.sessions`, `.user-data`

### What TO Do
- ✅ **ALWAYS** use centralized `ensureAuthForTarget()` for login/OTP
- ✅ **ALWAYS** validate inputs before enqueuing jobs
- ✅ **ALWAYS** return normalized responses via `normalizer.js`
- ✅ **ALWAYS** track stages with `jobCtx.setStage()`
- ✅ **ALWAYS** close pages with `releasePage()` in finally
- ✅ **ALWAYS** use `gotoFast()` over `page.goto()`
- ✅ **ALWAYS** extract selectors to `providers/forusall/config.js`
- ✅ **ALWAYS** write tests for new features (≥80% coverage)
- ✅ **ALWAYS** use structured logging (`log.event()`)
- ✅ **ALWAYS** document complex logic with comments

